course: dictionary
lesson: 2359
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. Cucumber is a noun. It can mean the long, thin, green vegetable with a cool, watery inside, or the plant it grows on. «Cats jump at a cucumber placed silently behind them» is about the vegetable, because you can place a vegetable behind someone.
explain: Words also appear in set phrases. «As cool as a cucumber» does not mean the vegetable is cold. It means someone is very calm, even when things are tense. Read the whole phrase as one unit, and do not swap in the meaning of each separate word.
explain: The same thing can have different names depending on who uses it. «To a botanist a fruit is the part that holds the seeds, so tomatoes, cucumbers, peppers and pumpkins are fruits», but cooks call them vegetables. Scientists and cooks use the word for different reasons, so check which meaning the writer is using.
fact: Cucumber is a noun: one cucumber, two cucumbers.
fact: A cucumber is a long, thin, green vegetable with a cool, watery inside, often eaten raw in salads or sandwiches.
fact: Cucumber can also mean the plant the vegetable grows on.
fact: To a botanist, a fruit is the part of a plant that holds the seeds, so cucumbers are fruits in plant science.
fact: Pickles, also called gherkins, are small pickled cucumbers.
exercise: «Cats jump at a cucumber placed silently behind them.» What is a cucumber here? | A kind of cat | A loud noise in the kitchen | A tall tree in a forest | *A long, thin, green vegetable
exercise: Mum says, «The cucumber has climbed right up the garden fence.» What does cucumber mean here? | A snake in the grass | A pickle in a jar | *The plant it grows on | A tomato on the vine
exercise: Why is a cucumber called a fruit by a botanist? | Because it is very long | *Because it has seeds inside | Because it is sweet like an apple | Because it grows on a tree
test: «As cool as a cucumber» describes someone who is: | Very cold | Very green | Very watery | *Very calm
test: Which word is the plural of cucumber? | cucumbern | cucumberes | cucumbies | *cucumbers
exam: «A giant snail rasps through cucumber with a tongue of thousands of tiny teeth.» What does cucumber mean here? | A jar of pickles | The flower of the plant | *The green vegetable | A kind of snail
